  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_933596d1",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a young girl with green hair (symbolizing youth and perceived immaturity) against text that contrasts her being 'not old enough to choose own bed time or daily diet' with being 'old enough to choose to be trans or gender fluid or non-binary'. This creates a false equivalence and implies that gender identity choices are somehow more significant or 'adult' than basic life decisions like diet or sleep, which is a harmful oversimplification. The meme uses the visual of a child to frame the discussion of gender identity in a way that can be perceived as mocking or infantilizing, potentially reinforcing harmful stereotypes about transgender and non-binary individuals. It may contribute to the perception that gender identity is a 'choice' rather than a deeply personal and complex aspect of identity, which can be damaging to the community. The overall intent is to provoke a reaction by highlighting a perceived contradiction, but in doing so, it risks spreading misinformation and contributing to stigma.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_38dc0250"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
